# The fifth codegen fixture: what the program prints.
#
# Every fixture so far was worth a number, and the gate compared the exit
# status. This one writes bytes, which is a stronger observable and the
# one a compiler is eventually judged by: the gate compares stdout as
# well.
#
# `print` of a literal is the whole of it. This slice does not build an
# iyi `String` - a bytesize, a length and the bytes - because nothing
# here asks a string for anything. It writes the bytes the literal
# holds, which is all `print` of a literal does.

require "../../../src/iyi/prelude"

print "hello from the port\n"
print "two lines, one of them with a tab:\there\n"
__iyi_exit(3)
